  "result": "Perfect! All 81 tests pass. I've successfully added line discount support:\n\n**Features added:**\n\n1. **Discount validation** - discountPercent must be a number between 0 and 100 (decimals like 12.5 are valid)\n   - Returns `DISCOUNT_INVALID` for invalid values\n\n2. **createInvoice** - now accepts optional `discountPercent` in line input\n   - Validates the value\n   - Stores it on the line if provided\n   - Omits it if not provided\n\n3. **addLine** - accepts optional `discountPercent`\n   - Validates it\n   - Updates discount on existing lines if provided\n   - Preserves existing discount if not provided in the update\n\n4. **invoiceTotals** - now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`\n   - Calculates discount for each line: `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n   - Sums all line discounts\n   - `total = subtotal - discount`\n   - **Clamps total at 0** (project-wide rule: no computed amount goes below 0)\n\n5. **renderInvoiceText** - displays discounts nicely\n   - Shows discount percent and amount on lines: `(10% off: -\u20ac17.00)`\n   - Shows subtotal, discount, and total when discounts present\n   - Shows simple total when no discounts\n\n**Test coverage (16 new discount-specific tests):**\n- Valid/invalid discounts in createInvoice and addLine\n- Decimal discount support\n- Edge cases (0%, 100% discounts)\n- Discount calculation and summation\n- Clamping at 0\n- Mixed discounts across multiple lines\n- Render output with/without discounts",
